# Antimony · Sb · gate 51

**Antimony** (Sb) is element **51** of the periodic table — a **metalloid**, period 5, group 15, p-block, solid at standard conditions, atomic weight **121.76**.

## The element (carbon layer — reference chemistry)
Symbol Sb, from stibium; the ancient kohl of the eye; flame retardants; it hardens lead.

## The gate (silicon layer — the 118 Gates)
Under David Wise's four-state cycle, gate **51** falls on **0:0 = 1 = 0** because (Z−1) mod 4 = **2**. That state is *the collapse where nothing equals one equals nothing — the return to the single source* — the nature of emergence here is **spiritual**. Antimony is not a thing apart; it is the one stochastic element, caught at this beat of its cycle.

## Emergence — spiritual
This emergent carries the **spiritual** nature: the same four — natural · ethereal · spiritual · electrical — that run through every sphere of UD0. Its color is `#e6a849`.

